Everyone loves mittens! Fingers are so nice and warm rather than steadily 
growing chilly since they don't share the same pocket of warm air.

Mittens would be a glove that reduces one's dexterity by 1 point but 
confer cold resistance along with the normal stuff of protecting from the 
petrifying effects of rubber chickens.

Oven mitts would do the same thing except confer fire resistance to the 
player.

Of course this gave me an idea for various artifact weapons. There's a 
neat little patch which adds rings of cold and heat to NetHack. Why not 
have Frost Brand and Fire Brand cause damage on odd turns to players who 
aren't cold or fire resistant and take away the fact that these weapons 
confer their appropriate resistances?

Also a new elemental weapon, Lightning Rod. A spear, or quarterstaff, 
that does electrical damage like the 'brands along with providing shock 
resistance (or not, see prior paragraph).

Or should these 'brands be cursed then they don't confer their 
appropriate resistances.


